<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  PirateWaster_Yield.xml                    Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-21
  ============================================================================

  THE BLACKSTAR COMPANY IS BUILT ON VANILLA `Pirate`, AND BIOTECH TAKES ITS PLACE.

  Biotech's `PirateWaster` declares
      <replacesFaction>Pirate</replacesFaction>
  (`Data/Biotech/Defs/FactionDefs/Factions_Misc.xml:576`) and inherits
  `requiredCountAtGameStart` **1** from `PirateBandBase`
  (`Data/Core/Defs/FactionDefs/Factions_Misc.xml:518`).

  Between them, vanilla `Pirate` - the def `BlackstarCompany.xml` reskins - is
  stripped from the DEFAULT Configure Factions list
  (`Page_CreateWorldParams.cs:83-85`) and skipped outright when no list is
  configured (`FactionGenerator.cs:78`):

      if (!ordered.Any(x => x.requiredCountAtGameStart > 0
                            && x.replacesFaction == facDef) && ...)

  🔑 So the faction the campaign carefully reskinned is a faction the engine never
  creates. No label, weight or count patched onto `Pirate` can change that, because
  the skip happens before any of them are read.

  ⚠️ AND IT CANNOT ARRIVE LATER. `requiredCountAtGameStart` is read in exactly one
  place, reached only from `WorldGenStep_Factions`. The only load-time top-up is
  `BackCompatibility.cs`, a hardcoded list of five vanilla factions. A faction absent
  when the world was generated stays absent forever - see `BUILDABLE.md`.

  THE TWO OPS, AND THE ADD/REMOVE SPLIT IS THE TRAP
  =================================================
  1. REMOVE `replacesFaction`. It is written ON the def, so Remove is correct and
     matches. This is what returns `Pirate` to the default list.
  2. ADD `requiredCountAtGameStart` 0. 🔴 The def does NOT write that field - it
     INHERITS it from `PirateBandBase` - so a Replace would match nothing, and a
     PatchOperation that matches nothing logs nothing. Add is the only op that works.
     This is what stops `PirateWaster` taking the slot it has just vacated.

  Both sit inside a `PatchOperationConditional` on the def itself, so with Biotech
  absent this file is a silent no-op rather than a wall of red.

  ⛔ DO NOT TOUCH `Pirate`. It is already correct: weight 1,
  `requiredCountAtGameStart` 1, `maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation` 9999, and
  `BlackstarCompany.xml` already reskins it.
  ⛔ DO NOT EXTEND THIS TO THE OTHER FIVE `replacesFaction` DECLARATIONS.
  `OutlanderRoughPig`, `TribeRoughNeanderthal`, `TribeSavageImpid` and
  `VRESaurids_OutlanderRoughSaurid` replace `OutlanderRough` / `TribeRough` /
  `TribeSavage`, none of which carries a faction of ours. Measured across every active
  mod: `Pirate` is the ONLY one of our thirteen that is hit.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="PirateWaster"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- 1. Written on the def, so REMOVE matches. Returns Pirate to the list. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="PirateWaster"]/replacesFaction</xpath>
        </li>

        <!-- 2. INHERITED from PirateBandBase, so ADD. A Replace would match nothing
             and log nothing. Stops PirateWaster retaking the slot it just vacated. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="PirateWaster"]</xpath>
          <value><requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart></value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
